 \"What political party is Senator Atkinson a part of?\", \"slot_hint\": \"political_party\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 87, \"text\": \"Archibald Atkinson Archibald Atkinson (September 15, 1792 – January 7, 1872) was a U.S.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d00\", \"start\": 88, \"end\": 117, \"text\": \"Representative from Virginia.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d00\", \"start\": 118, \"end\": 196, \"text\": \"Born in Isle of Wight County, Virginia, Atkinson received a liberal education.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d00\", \"start\": 197, \"end\": 324, \"text\": \"He attended the law department of the College of William & Mary (now the Marshall-Wythe School of Law), Williamsburg, Virginia.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d00\", \"start\": 325, \"end\": 358, \"text\": \"He served during the War of 1812.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d00\", \"start\": 359, \"end\": 433, \"text\": \"He was admitted to the bar and commenced practice in Smithfield, Virginia.\"}, \"D1S7\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d00\", \"start\": 434, \"end\": 554, \"text\": \"He was a member of the Virginia House of Delegates 1815–1817 and 1828–1831, and served in the Virginia Senate 1839–1843.\"}, \"D1S8\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d00\", \"start\": 555, \"end\": 639, \"text\": \"Atkinson was elected as a Democrat to the Twenty-eighth, Twenty-ninth, and Thirtieth\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 106, \"text\": \"Jason Atkinson Jason Atkinson (born November 6, 1970) is an American politician in the US state of Oregon.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d01\", \"start\": 107, \"end\": 169, \"text\": \"The Republican grew up in the Southern Oregon city of Ashland.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d01\", \"start\": 170, \"end\": 238, \"text\": \"He served as a senator in the Oregon State Senate from 2001 to 2013.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d01\", \"start\": 239, \"end\": 363, \"text\": \"He ran unsuccessfully for the Republican nomination for Governor of Oregon in 2006, but was reelected to the Senate in 2008.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d01\", \"start\": 364, \"end\": 473, \"text\": \"He stated his intention to run in the 2010 Oregon gubernatorial election, but withdrew from the race in 2009.\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d01\", \"start\": 474, \"end\": 562, \"text\": \"In 1998, Atkinson was elected to his first public office as a member of the Oregon House\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 62, \"text\": \"Check out iVoterGuide JavaScript is disabled in your browser .\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d02\", \"start\": 63, \"end\": 113, \"text\": \"Please enable JavaScript to use this application .\"}, \"D4S1\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d03\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 63, \"text\": \"our professional staff of editors , writers , and researchers .\"}, \"D4S2\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d03\", \"start\": 64, \"end\": 126, \"text\": \"Click here to contact our editorial staff or report an error .\"}, \"D4S3\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d03\", \"start\": 127, \"end\": 166, \"text\": \"For media inquiries ,